  "request": {
    "spec": "Redesign the identity key: identityKey = SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)); duplicate detection (409) uses this key, still ignoring owners flagged deleted and still applying the email-domain blocklist first. This changes existing behaviour: the soft-match must now trigger when the identityKey differs but soundex(lastName) and postcode match. Because the telephone is part of the key, two owners with the same lastName and postcode but DIFFERENT telephones are no longer a hard household duplicate: they are created as a soft match (not rejected with 409). Duplicate detection is now the single identity key, so the separate household-duplicate 409 block from the computed householdId no longer applies.",
    "prompt": "Implement the following change to the application so that it fully satisfies\nthe specification and all existing and new tests pass. Run the test suite and\nmake it green before finishing.\n\nRedesign the identity key: identityKey = SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)); duplicate detection (409) uses this key, still ignoring owners flagged deleted and still applying the email-domain blocklist first. This changes existing behaviour: the soft-match must now trigger when the identityKey differs but soundex(lastName) and postcode match. Because the telephone is part of the key, two owners with the same lastName and postcode but DIFFERENT telephones are no longer a hard household duplicate: they are created as a soft match (not rejected with 409). Duplicate detection is now the single identity key, so the separate household-duplicate 409 block from the computed householdId no longer applies.\n"
  },
