    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS, 2/2 tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI agreed with the finding and fixed the duplication:\n\n- **Added `model/Hashing.java`** \u2014 a small public helper holding the single lower-case hex SHA-256 primitive, placed in `model` beside `Owner`/`OwnerIdentity`/`Soundex`, matching the codebase's \"shared derivation lives in `model`\" convention.\n- **`OwnerIdentity`** now calls `Hashing.sha256Hex(...)` and its private copy (plus the now-unused `MessageDigest`/charset imports) is gone.\n- **`OwnerHousehold`** now calls `Hashing.sha256Hex(...)` for the householdId and its byte-for-byte-identical private copy is removed. This class is in `rest.function.owner`, which already imports freely from `model`, so no cycle.\n\nOn the reviewer's optional note: I left **`AssignCustomerCode.hash8`** as-is. It's a genuinely different helper (upper-case, truncated to 8 chars, short-circuits the loop early) rather than the same primitive, so folding it into `Hashing` would either require a second method or a lossy `sha256Hex(...).substring(0,8).toUpperCase()` rewrite \u2014 not the duplication the finding targeted, and outside the scope of keeping this change focused.\n\nTests re-run clean: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
